# The design system, until Phase C converts it in place (`DEC-21`) -- the same boundary
# eslint.config.js draws, and drawn here for a sharper reason.
#
# `frontend/design-system/` is the signed-off visual language (`DEC-8`) and the `.prompt.md`
# files beside each component are the only record of when not to use it. Running a formatter
# over all of that today would rewrite the record and turn every conversion diff in `UI-1d`
# through `UI-1h` into a reformat with a conversion hidden inside it. Each of those tasks takes
# its own folder off this list as it converts.
design-system/
# ...except the TypeScript the conversion produces, which is ordinary source and is formatted
# like the rest of it (`UI-1c`). `tokens.ts` is generated, and Prettier is what settles the
# argument between the generator's output and the formatter's opinion of it.
#
# The list maintains itself: a component `UI-1d` through `UI-1h` has converted is no longer a
# `.jsx`, so it is formatted the moment it is renamed. The hand-written `.d.ts` prop
# documentation stays out -- each folds into its component as that component converts, so
# reformatting it now is reformatting something on its way out.
!design-system/**/*.ts
!design-system/**/*.tsx
design-system/**/*.d.ts

# The API's shape, and the types generated from it (`UI-3a`). Both are written by a generator --
# `sonarium openapi` on one side of the repository and `npm run api:types` on the other -- and
# both are checked by comparing the committed file to what the generator produces today. A
# formatter in between would make that comparison a comparison of two formatters.
src/api/contract/
